24. Important Concept: Why the DB Subnet Is Private

The DB subnet:

10.0.2.0/24

does not have:

0.0.0.0/0 → Internet Gateway

Therefore, it isn't configured as a public subnet.

For a production design, you would typically have:

                    VPC
                     |
          +----------+----------+
          |                     |
          v                     v
     Public/App              Private/DB
     Subnet                   Subnet
          |                     |
          v                     v
        EC2                  Database
          |
          v
         IGW

And if the application in the public subnet needs to communicate with a database:

EC2
 |
 | Private IP
 v
DB Subnet
 |
 v
RDS / Database

You do not need an Internet Gateway route between the App and DB subnet. The VPC's local route provides communication between subnets in the same VPC.

