27. Optional AWS CLI Version

Once you understand the console workflow, the same architecture can be created with AWS CLI.

Create VPC
aws ec2 create-vpc \
  --cidr-block 10.0.0.0/16 \
  --tag-specifications \
  'ResourceType=vpc,Tags=[{Key=Name,Value=training-vpc}]'
Create App subnet
aws ec2 create-subnet \
  --vpc-id <VPC_ID> \
  --cidr-block 10.0.1.0/24 \
  --availability-zone us-east-1a \
  --tag-specifications \
  'ResourceType=subnet,Tags=[{Key=Name,Value=app-subnet}]'
Create DB subnet
aws ec2 create-subnet \
  --vpc-id <VPC_ID> \
  --cidr-block 10.0.2.0/24 \
  --availability-zone us-east-1b \
  --tag-specifications \
  'ResourceType=subnet,Tags=[{Key=Name,Value=db-subnet}]'
Create Internet Gateway
aws ec2 create-internet-gateway \
  --tag-specifications \
  'ResourceType=internet-gateway,Tags=[{Key=Name,Value=training-igw}]'
Attach IGW
aws ec2 attach-internet-gateway \
  --vpc-id <VPC_ID> \
  --internet-gateway-id <IGW_ID>
Create custom route table
aws ec2 create-route-table \
  --vpc-id <VPC_ID> \
  --tag-specifications \
  'ResourceType=route-table,Tags=[{Key=Name,Value=app-public-rt}]'
Create Internet route
aws ec2 create-route \
  --route-table-id <ROUTE_TABLE_ID> \
  --destination-cidr-block 0.0.0.0/0 \
  --gateway-id <IGW_ID>
Associate App subnet
aws ec2 associate-route-table \
  --route-table-id <ROUTE_TABLE_ID> \
  --subnet-id <APP_SUBNET_ID>

These CLI steps follow AWS's documented VPC creation, Internet Gateway, custom route-table, route, and subnet-association workflow.

The key concept to teach

The most important thing for students to understand is:

VPC
 |
 +--- Subnet
       |
       +--- Route Table
              |
              +--- Route
                     |
                     +--- Target

For your App subnet:

App Subnet
     |
     v
Custom Route Table
     |
     +--- 10.0.0.0/16 → local
     |
     +--- 0.0.0.0/0 → Internet Gateway

That combination, plus a public IP on the EC2 instance and appropriate security-group rules, is what gives the EC2 instance internet connectivity.

For your DB subnet:

DB Subnet
     |
     v
Private/Main Route Table
     |
     +--- 10.0.0.0/16 → local

This gives you the foundation for the next stage: App EC2 → private DB/RDS, followed by NAT Gateway, ALB, and eventually converting the whole architecture into Terraform modules.
